## Setup

Install [Homebrew](https://brew.sh), then run in the repository:

```sh
brew install mise gh
mise install                           # node and pnpm from mise.toml
mise exec -- pnpm install              # dependencies from pnpm-lock.yaml
git config core.hooksPath .githooks
gh extension install github/gh-stack   # optional: stacked PRs
```

mise installs the exact Node and pnpm in `mise.toml` and checks them against `mise.lock`. Add
`eval "$(mise activate zsh)"` to `~/.zshrc` to put them on `PATH` in every shell; otherwise
prefix commands with `mise exec --`. pnpm refuses to run with any other Node or pnpm version
(`devEngines` in `package.json`). The git hook runs the checks before each push. `gh stack` is
optional: it helps to open and update stacked PRs.

Editor: TypeScript 7 ships its language server in `tsc`. Run it as
`node_modules/.bin/tsc --lsp --stdio`; in VS Code, install the `TypeScriptTeam.native-preview`
extension. The oxc extension, or `oxlint --lsp` and `oxfmt --lsp`, shows lint and format results.

## Commands

```sh
scripts/check                 # every quality gate: lockfile, format, lint, types, unused code, tests
pnpm start Ada                # run the program (Node runs the .ts files directly)
pnpm test                     # tests only
pnpm exec vitest run -t "greets the world"   # one test by name
pnpm fmt                      # format
pnpm lint --fix               # fix what lint can fix
pnpm typecheck                # type check only
```

`scripts/check` is the single list of gates. The git hook and CI run it too. CI also runs
pnpm's supply-chain policy for the lockfile (job `lockfile-policy`), which needs the registry.

